@vsm 1.0
// orphaned_tasks_audit_2026-08-02.vsm
// Author: Claude fork (audit), dispatched by [O] same-session, 2026-08-02.
// rmw3's question: "antes que implementáramos state.db, formulamos varias tareas que nunca se
// ejecutaron... sería bueno tomar esta hebra y ver qué otras tareas quedaron descritas y nunca
// se ejecutaron, por que si seguimos encubriéndolas, vamos en algún momento quedar con el agua
// al cuello." Trigger: mid-session discovery that dynamic_resources_all_lxc.spec.vsm's TIER-2
// was ratified 2026-07-03 and never built, unnoticed for a month.

audit(ORPHANED-TASKS-2026-08-02) {

  timeline_finding: "TASKS.vsm itself predates state.db by ~7 weeks (first commit a4f5a36,
      2026-04-08; state.db canon established 2026-05-30, commit 0b38949 'RULES.md + onboard.sh').
      MASTER_PLAN.vsm (a SEPARATE, later planning doc) was created 2026-06-23 and retired
      2026-07-31 — 'before state.db' in rmw3's framing likely maps more precisely to 'before the
      2026-07-02/07-03 gap-audit + spec-driven-task discipline took hold', which is when almost
      all of the genuinely-orphaned items below cluster (see below). TASK_INDEX.vsm no longer
      exists on disk (already retired per CLAUDE.md). A pre-built tool exists for exactly this
      purpose — scripts/state/tasks_reconcile.py (DEBT-42) — but its parser is stale: it only
      recognizes the OLD single-letter task(X) format and 4-status vocabulary, so it counted 33
      tasks total when TASKS.vsm actually has 314. Did not fix it (out of scope) — flagged as its
      own small finding, not registered as a task (low value: this audit already did the job by
      hand once; recommend fixing the parser only if this kind of sweep becomes routine).",

  method: "Parsed all 314 task() blocks programmatically (name + status field, handling both
      status=X and status: X syntax — the tasks_reconcile.py tool's regex only catches the
      former, which is why it undercounted). 314 total, 206 straightforwardly done/closed, 108
      initial non-done candidates. Cross-checked against the 2026-07-30/07-31 CLAUDE.md backlog
      resync and DEBT_CLOSURE_PLAN.vsm ('HISTORICAL — all 5 waves executed and closed') to bulk-
      exclude the pre-existing legacy/superseded W1-W4 wave cluster (~50 entries, already
      correctly self-labeled or covered by that prior resync — spot-checked 2 live, both
      confirmed done: W3-OLLAMA-MIGRATE, S3-STAR-HASH-BUG). Remaining 52 candidates individually
      read; ~30 verified live (grep source, ssh/pct exec, systemctl, direct API calls) rather than
      trusted from doc text alone — same discipline as the 2026-07-30 theme resync.",

  classification_counts: {
    total_task_blocks: 314,
    a_done_but_stale: 9,        // status field corrected in TASKS.vsm directly, see below
    b_genuinely_open: 6,        // new audit_2026_08_02 dispatch-ready notes added to existing tasks
    c_correctly_gated_not_debt: 4,  // FIERRO-FULL-BODY, PAPER-2-VARIETY, S1-PHI-DOWN-GUARD, IAC-TERRAFORM
    ambiguous_needs_follow_up: 2,   // AUTOIMMUNE-TEST (caveat), ENTROPY-SATURATION-REVIEW parts B/C
    skipped_already_tracked_this_session: 4,  // S1-ISOLATION-RELAY-ARCH, S3-ALLOC-NATS-CRASHLOOP-UNROOTED,
                                                // STATE-DB-101-IP-CANON-MISMATCH, LXC113-ELIMINATION-PAUSED
    not_individually_re_audited: ">30",  // the legacy W1-W4 cluster, bulk-classified via
                                          // DEBT_CLOSURE_PLAN.vsm's own historical status + 2 live spot-checks
  },

  // ── (a) DONE BUT TRACKING STALE — fixed in place, no new task ────────────────────
  a_findings: [
    "AA (paper §Theory Markov) — §2.5 landed in attractor_convergence v0.8, memory confirms.",
    "STATE-CANON-DOCS-TASKS-FOCUS + STATE-CANON-FRESHNESS-RECONCILER — both closed by the
     2026-07-27/07-30 state-canon-mcp patch cycles (memory project_state_canon_mcp), TASKS.vsm
     headers still said 'dispatched'.",
    "OLLAMA-UPGRADE-110 — the ONE explicitly pending sub-item (num_ctx=1024 live test) run live
     during this audit: SUCCEEDED (6.2s, real response). Note updated with evidence.",
    "EXP-NB-01-FIX — memory project_exp_nb01_vos_nano documents the showstopper + all 3 scaffolds
     already fixed; TASKS.vsm still said open.",
    "DIVERSE-VERIFIER — vsf-diverse-verify.timer + .service confirmed live on n02 host.",
    "TRIAGE-EVIDENCE-RULE — _clf_merkle_break_evidence confirmed replacing the old function in
     vsf_s5_agent.py, same-day commit 64748a7 as the task itself.",
    "AUTOIMMUNE-TEST — code exists (vsf_autoimmune.py, same commit 64748a7) but a live weekly
     systemd timer could not be confirmed within audit budget — marked done WITH a caveat, not
     fully closed. See ambiguous list.",
    "EXP-SOPLO-01 — most interesting case: results (fig_soplo_landauer.pdf/png,
     soplo_landauer_summary.json) date from commit 9c59e3d, 2026-06-18 — TWO WEEKS BEFORE the
     2026-07-02 gap-audit batch re-registered it as 'spec_ready_ds'. The gap-audit session that
     was itself trying to find undone work re-flagged something already finished, because it
     didn't check for prior results first. Worth remembering as a caution for this audit's own
     method too.",
  ],

  // ── (b) GENUINELY STILL OPEN — dispatch-ready notes added to the EXISTING task() blocks ──
  b_findings: [
    "EXP-LL-01-P1 (Ω Doughnut) — design done 2026-07-02 (omega_doughnut_design.vsm §5, P1a-P1d),
     omega_econ.py never created, over a month later. Sibling tasks from the same batch
     (EXP-LL-01-COPPER, EXP-LL-01-COUPLE) both landed within days — this one specifically fell
     through.",
    "P3-SEED-TO-SKELETON (open_systems paper) — skeleton done 2026-07-02, main.tex unchanged
     since (git log confirms), the named 'next writing session' never happened.",
    "ITEM-21-DESIGN (VSM recursion, s1-santiago pilot) — design done 2026-07-02 with 5
     DS-executable phases (item21_nested_vsm_interface.vsm), its own blocker (EXP-S2-01) IS done,
     but the pilot was never dispatched. No s1-santiago implementation found anywhere.",
    "EXP-S4-01-STRESS — blocked on brecha(PHI-UP-PIPELINE), which is now RESOLVED (Track A closed
     2026-07-14 + S4-MULTI-S1 Phase 1/3 done 2026-07-31). Re-run is unblocked and was never
     re-attempted.",
    "DYN-LLM-GRANT — P1 done 2026-07-02, P2 (startup assert) + P3 (state.db-backing) explicitly
     named 'next', never touched since. Same subsystem (s3_resource_alloc.py) as TWO other things
     found stalled today (dynamic_resources_all_lxc.spec.vsm's TIER-2, and the vsf-s3-alloc NATS
     crash-loop) — recommend one bundled DS dispatch touching that file once, not three.",
    "S4-MULTI-S1 Phase 2 — HIGH VALUE, immediately actionable: its blocker (OLLAMA-UPGRADE-110's
     num_ctx>256 crash) is the SAME thing just confirmed cleared live in the (a) list above. Phase
     2 (S4_SYNTH cross-domain synthesis + routing_signal) has zero remaining blocker as of this
     audit and can be dispatched to DS immediately.",
  ],

  // ── ambiguous / needs a fast follow-up, not fully classified either way ──────────
  ambiguous: [
    "AUTOIMMUNE-TEST's recurring weekly schedule — code exists, live cron/timer wiring
     unconfirmed (SSH filesystem sweep timed out before completing; not a negative result, an
     inconclusive one).",
    "ENTROPY-SATURATION-REVIEW parts (B)/(C) — part (A) checkpoint persistence CONFIRMED done in
     kernel_step.rs. Whether (B) (drop H_T from the margin danger set in omega_validator.rs) also
     landed was not checked. (C) is rmw3's own semantics call (4-symbol alphabet width), not
     DS-executable regardless.",
  ],

  // ── correctly gated, NOT debt — excluded from further action ─────────────────────
  correctly_gated: [
    "FIERRO-FULL-BODY + PAPER-2-VARIETY — both explicitly wait on rmw3's own send-timing decision
     (ITEM_11-class, memory project_paper_attractor: 'send held until systems validated'). Known,
     not forgotten — rmw3 IS the gate.",
    "S1-PHI-DOWN-GUARD — gated on the BBH-integration R6, which CLAUDE.md's own current backlog
     table still lists as deliberately open ('not yet clear how to approach reconsidering it').",
    "IAC-TERRAFORM — explicitly gated 'post-public-release', no urgency claimed by its own text.",
  ],

  method_caveat: "This audit covered the 108-candidate non-done set exhaustively at the
      classification level, but individual live verification depth varied — the highest-value/
      most-ambiguous items got full SSH/grep verification (~15 items), the rest were classified
      by content reading + cross-reference against memory and known session history. The bulk
      W1-W4 legacy cluster (~50 entries) was NOT read individually — classified via
      DEBT_CLOSURE_PLAN.vsm's own 'HISTORICAL, all 5 waves closed' status plus 2 spot-checks. If
      a specific W1-W4 item matters later, verify it individually rather than trusting this bulk
      classification blindly — same standing rule as everywhere else in this project.",

  next: "The 6 (b) items now carry dispatch-ready audit_2026_08_02 notes directly in their
      existing TASKS.vsm task() blocks (not new task names — updated in place, since the names
      already existed and described the right scope, just needed the 'why still open' + 'what to
      do' made explicit). rmw3/Claude to sequence these against the S1-ISOLATION-RELAY-ARCH queue
      already waiting on DS. S4-MULTI-S1 Phase 2 is the standout quick win — zero remaining
      blocker, confirmed live during this audit.",
}
